# Reports of the undefined-behaviour sanitizer that are known and tracked.
# One line a site: <check>:<function>, or <check>:<source file> where the function
# is inlined into its callers and its name does not reach the report. A line leaves
# this file with the change that fixes its site. The file holds no line when no
# site is known.
#
# Used by the sanitizer job of .github/workflows/ci.yml and by hand:
#   UBSAN_OPTIONS=halt_on_error=1:suppressions=$PWD/test/sanitizer_suppressions/ubsan
#
# montgomery_reduce, src/crypto/latticebp/commitment.cpp: a product taken in 32 bits.
# The function is inlined, so the line names its file.
signed-integer-overflow:crypto/latticebp/commitment.cpp
# src/crypto/sha256.cpp: an offset added to a null pointer on a write of nothing.
pointer-overflow:CSHA256::Write
